# Work Center & Section Calculation Engine Rework Plan

## 1. Executive Summary & Core Principles
* **Immutable Snapshot History:** Calculations are completely decoupled from operational tables (`production_work_centers`, `production_work_center_sections`). Every calculation run produces a new immutable record in history tables.
* **Smart Debounce / Countdown Engine:** Micro-actions (assigning personnel, adjusting shift workers, machine mapping) trigger a configurable countdown (e.g., 5–10 mins) instead of immediately firing heavy queries.
* **Targeted Section & Rollup Scope:** Only changed/impacted sections in a countdown window are recalculated. Work Center calculations aggregate the latest state of all sections plus WC-level resources.
* **Shift-Anchored Manual Production:** Manual production is no longer a static number on a section. It is tied to dedicated teams/batches anchored to specific shifts, whether composed of internal employees or external worker allocations.
* **Clean Relational Schema:** Queryable high-level metrics are stored as database columns; detailed cost breakdowns, worker lists, and shift metadata live inside structured `calculation_details` JSON.

