### Countdown Configuration Rules
1. **Per-Work Center Timer:** `calculation_countdown_minutes` is a **required field** in the Work Center create and edit form. Every Work Center independently configures its own countdown duration. There is no system-wide default — it must be set by the user on creation.
2. **Change Duration Modal:** When **no countdown is currently active**, a dedicated **"Change Countdown Duration"** button is visible on the Work Center page. Clicking it opens a modal allowing the authorized user to update the duration. This button is hidden / disabled while a countdown is actively ticking.
3. **Countdown Cannot Be Cancelled:** Once a countdown is triggered (by a micro-action or a form save), it **cannot be stopped or cancelled**. A configuration change has already been committed to the database and will impact calculated rates — the recalculation MUST run. The only path to accelerate it is the **"Recalculate Now"** manual bypass button, which fires the calculation immediately before the timer expires. This is an acceleration, not a cancellation — the pending changes are still fully calculated.

