### Step 3: Work Center Roll-up & Overhead Application
*(Assuming this is the only section in the Work Center for this example.)*

* **WC Daily Capacity** = Section Daily Capacity = **1,912.5 units**
* **WC Hourly Capacity** = Section Hourly Capacity = **155 units/hr**
* **WC Unique Operating Hours** = 15.0 hrs
* **WC Daily Overhead Cost** (flat, entered in WC form) = **$1,200.00/day**
* **WC Overhead Cost Per Hour** (computed reference) = $\$1,200.00 / 15.0 = \mathbf{\$80.00/\text{hr}}$
* **WC Total Daily Operating Cost** = Labor Daily + Machine Daily + Overhead:
  $$\text{WC Total Daily Cost} = \text{WC Daily Labor} + \text{WC Daily Machine Expense} + \$1,200.00$$
  *(Full labor and machine cost details are demonstrated in the overlapping shift walkthrough in Section 8.)*

> **Note on Overhead:** Overhead is always stored and entered as a **flat daily amount**. The `overhead_cost_per_hour` displayed in the UI is derived by dividing the flat daily amount by `WC Unique Operating Hours` — it is a computed display value only, not stored separately.

