## 7. Complete Labor Costing Engine

### A. Internal Employee Labor Costing (HRMS Grounded)
Internal employees have individual personalized salaries fetched from the HRMS module:
1. **Source:** Look up employee's **Net Monthly Salary** (net monthly payables) from HRMS pay structure.
2. **Daily Rate (Standard 30 Days):**
   $$\text{Daily Salary} = \frac{\text{Net Monthly Salary}}{30}$$
3. **Individual Hourly Rate:**
   $$\text{Employee Hourly Rate} = \frac{\text{Daily Salary}}{\text{Assigned Shift Effective Hours}} = \frac{\text{Net Monthly Salary}}{30 \times \text{Shift Effective Hours}}$$
4. **Daily Cost in Section:**
   $$\text{Employee Daily Cost} = \text{Employee Hourly Rate} \times \text{Shift Effective Hours} = \text{Daily Salary}$$

> **Intentional Design Decision (Fixed CTC / Salary Model):**
> It is completely intentional that an employee's derived hourly rate depends on the effective duration of the shift they are assigned to. Because employees are compensated on a fixed monthly CTC/salary, their daily liability to the company is fixed ($\text{Salary} \div 30$). If they work a 6-hour shift, their effective hourly burn rate is higher than if they work an 8-hour shift, but their total daily cost impact to the section remains identical.

### B. External Worker Labor Costing (Pay Grade Headcount)
1. **Source:** Hourly rate from `production_external_worker_pay_grades` $\times$ number of workers.
2. **Allocation Hourly Rate:**
   $$\text{Allocation Hourly Rate} = \text{number\_of\_workers} \times \text{pay\_grade\_hourly\_rate}$$
3. **Allocation Daily Cost:**
   $$\text{Allocation Daily Cost} = \text{Allocation Hourly Rate} \times \text{Shift Effective Hours}$$

### C. HRMS Integration & Fallback Handling
When querying an employee's Net Monthly Salary from the HRMS module:
1. **Configured Salary Found:** Proceed with standard salary-to-daily derivation ($\text{Salary} \div 30$).
2. **Missing Salary in HRMS:** The calculation engine does NOT crash or abort. It records a labor cost of `$0.00` for that employee, marks the record with a `⚠️ Missing HRMS Salary` warning flag in the `calculation_details` JSON payload, and surfaces an alert on the Work Center roster.
3. **HRMS Module Unavailable:** The engine falls back to the most recent cached salary snapshot on the employee record. If no historical snapshot exists, it defaults to `$0.00` with an outage warning flag logged in `production_work_center_activity_logs`.

